This product is a fork of enzo, an open source 3D software for procedural
modeling in VFX or animation.

  Upstream project: https://github.com/parkerbritt/enzo
  Upstream author:  ParkerBritt
  Upstream website: https://enzo3d.com
  Upstream docs:    https://parkerbritt.github.io/enzo/

The original enzo source code, its engine architecture, node system, data model,
parameter system, user interface and documentation are the work of ParkerBritt
and are used here under the terms of the MIT license reproduced in the LICENSE
file at the root of this repository.

The macOS port, the asynchronous cooking scheduler, the timeline, the simulation
node family, the user node authoring support, the viewport work and the interface
redesign were carried out for this fork by the Helix contributors.

The scene format is unchanged, so files saved by Helix open in enzo and the other
way round.

